# CYS-MAL — Cys-S to maleimide post-Michael adduct (3-thiosuccinimide)
#
# Hand-authored link CIF for PyKeko covalent-ligand workflow.
# Family F5 of the plan-doc taxonomy: covers maleimide-warhead probes,
# fluorescent labels (Alexa Fluor maleimides, fluorescein maleimides),
# antibody-drug conjugate linkers (the workhorse for ADCs), and the
# tens of thousands of bioconjugation probes that use maleimide as the
# Cys-targeting handle.
#
# Mechanism:
#   maleimide (5-ring with C=C) + Cys-S⁻ →
#   3-thiosuccinimide (5-ring with C-C, Cβ has S, Cα gained H)
#
# Like F1 acrylamide, this is a Michael addition: the Cα=Cβ goes from
# double → single, the Cα receives a Michael proton, both carbons
# retype sp²→sp³. UNLIKE F1, the warhead is constrained to a 5-ring
# which is preserved through the reaction (ring stays closed, just
# becomes saturated). Cβ keeps its single H pre→post; only Cα gains
# the new H.
#
# Geometric difference vs F1 CYS-ACR.cif:
#   * Cβ's "Cγ" position is occupied by the ring-closing carbonyl-C
#     (the "second" carbonyl in the maleimide / succinimide ring).
#     That carbonyl is bonded to the SAME amide-N as Cα's carbonyl,
#     and that's the ring-closure signature the detector uses to
#     distinguish F5 from F1 (which has no ring).
#   * SG-Cβ-Cring angle (where Cring = ring's other carbonyl-C) is
#     close to tetrahedral but slightly compressed by the 5-ring strain.
#   * No planarity restraint — sp3 succinimide ring is non-planar.
#
# PLACEHOLDER TOKENS substituted at runtime:
#   <LIG> ← ligand 3-letter (or 5-char) CCD code
#   <CB>  ← Cβ atom-id (gets the SG)
#   <CA>  ← Cα atom-id (the other ring vinyl C; gains the Michael H)
#   <CG>  ← ring-closing carbonyl-C on Cβ's side (the "second"
#            maleimide carbonyl; the detector resolves it as the
#            non-Cα carbon neighbour of Cβ that is itself a carbonyl-C)
#   <CO>  ← Cα-side carbonyl-C atom-id
#   <N>   ← amide-N atom-id (shared between both ring carbonyls)
#   <O>   ← Cα-side carbonyl-O atom-id
#   <HCA> ← H to add on Cα (alkene pre-reaction input only)
#
# References:
#   ~/Moorhen/docs/refs/nicholls-modelling-2021.pdf — CCP4-ML link-CIF format
#   ~/Moorhen/docs/covalent-ligand-plan.md §2.5 (F5 maleimide family)

data_link_CYS-MAL
_chem_link.id                CYS-MAL
_chem_link.name              "Cys-S to maleimide post-Michael adduct (3-thiosuccinimide)"
_chem_link.comp_id_1         CYS
_chem_link.mod_id_1          CYS-MAL-mod1
_chem_link.group_comp_1      L-peptide
_chem_link.comp_id_2         <LIG>
_chem_link.mod_id_2          CYS-MAL-mod2
_chem_link.group_comp_2      non-polymer

# ---- bonds: new S-Cβ single bond (sp3 S to sp3 C) ----
loop_
_chem_link_bond.atom_1_comp_id
_chem_link_bond.atom_id_1
_chem_link_bond.atom_2_comp_id
_chem_link_bond.atom_id_2
_chem_link_bond.type
_chem_link_bond.value_dist
_chem_link_bond.value_dist_esd
 1 SG    2 <CB>   single 1.81 0.02

# ---- angles around the new sp3 thioether linkage ----
# Cys side: standard sp3 S range.
# Ligand side: 5-ring constraint compresses tetrahedral angles slightly.
# SG-Cβ-Cα and SG-Cβ-Cring both target 112° (vs 113° in F1 acyclic).
loop_
_chem_link_angle.atom_1_comp_id
_chem_link_angle.atom_id_1
_chem_link_angle.atom_2_comp_id
_chem_link_angle.atom_id_2
_chem_link_angle.atom_3_comp_id
_chem_link_angle.atom_id_3
_chem_link_angle.value_angle
_chem_link_angle.value_angle_esd
 1 CB    1 SG    2 <CB>   100.0   3.0
 1 SG    2 <CB>  2 <CA>   112.0   2.0
 1 SG    2 <CB>  2 <CG>   112.0   2.0

# ---- soft torsion on the sp3-sp3 Cys-side hinge ----
# No torsion on the Cβ-Cα bond — that's locked by the 5-ring topology
# inside the ligand's own chem_comp.
loop_
_chem_link_tor.id
_chem_link_tor.atom_1_comp_id
_chem_link_tor.atom_id_1
_chem_link_tor.atom_2_comp_id
_chem_link_tor.atom_id_2
_chem_link_tor.atom_3_comp_id
_chem_link_tor.atom_id_3
_chem_link_tor.atom_4_comp_id
_chem_link_tor.atom_id_4
_chem_link_tor.value_angle
_chem_link_tor.value_angle_esd
_chem_link_tor.period
 sp3_sp3_cys_hinge 1 CA    1 CB    1 SG    2 <CB>   180.0  20.0  3


# =====================================================================
# Cys-side modification: delete HG (the thiol H)
# =====================================================================
data_mod_CYS-MAL-mod1
loop_
_chem_mod_atom.mod_id
_chem_mod_atom.function
_chem_mod_atom.atom_id
_chem_mod_atom.new_atom_id
_chem_mod_atom.new_type_symbol
_chem_mod_atom.new_type_energy
_chem_mod_atom.new_partial_charge
 CYS-MAL-mod1 delete HG . . . .


# =====================================================================
# Ligand-side modification — POST-PRODUCT 3-THIOSUCCINIMIDE INPUT BRANCH.
#
# Assumes the ligand chem_comp was deposited with the saturated
# 3-thiosuccinimide form already drawn. Unlike F1, there's no spare H
# on Cβ to delete — Cβ in the saturated form has S + Cα + Cring + H,
# all four bonded. The single H stays; the link just adds the SG bond
# at the chem_link level.
#
# The minimal mod2 for F5-post is therefore EMPTY (no atom/bond ops).
# We still need the data_mod_* block so the substituter doesn't break
# trying to swap in a non-existent file; just no operations inside.
#
# If the runtime detector instead matched the maleimide pre-Michael form
# (free probe SMILES with the ring C=C still drawn), use
# CYS-MAL-mod2-alkene.cif which:
#   (1) changes Cα=Cβ from double to single,
#   (2) adds a new H on Cα,
#   (3) retypes Cα and Cβ from sp2 to sp3.
# =====================================================================
data_mod_CYS-MAL-mod2
loop_
_chem_mod_atom.mod_id
_chem_mod_atom.function
_chem_mod_atom.atom_id
_chem_mod_atom.new_atom_id
_chem_mod_atom.new_type_symbol
_chem_mod_atom.new_type_energy
_chem_mod_atom.new_partial_charge
# No-op: F5 post-product input requires no atom changes on the ligand.
# Cβ in the saturated 3-thiosuccinimide form already has the correct
# bond list (Cα, ring-CO, H, will get S via link). The presence of
# this empty loop_ block is what the applier expects to find when it
# parses the mod2.
